        <item>
            <title>0.5.1</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 00:13:49 -0400</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/templetongroup/Kiki/releases/tag/v0.5.1</link>
            <sparkle:version>16</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# Kiki 0.5.1

Voice Studio is now a clear, guided three-step workflow:

- Read the complete enrollment passage at a larger 16-point size without scrolling.
- Record, preview, and save your voice with distinct controls and immediate confirmation.
- Install the local voice engine with accurate progress and plain-language instructions.
- See exactly why voice generation is unavailable and what step remains.
- Generate automatically unlocks when your saved voice, local engine, and text are ready.

This update also prevents recording playback from continuing after Save Voice and keeps every action button on one readable line.
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/templetongroup/Kiki/releases/download/v0.5.1/Kiki-0.5.1-macOS.zip" length="51212318" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="uXLSzopAx6wbVct3CD4bdrAlRnk09Xu4k/GuV/eT8TZ26WlzG+7GdlW2Y57hEcmADhSYBAusbLaG9Up316sECQ=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>0.5.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 23:11:21 -0400</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/templetongroup/Kiki/releases/tag/v0.5.0</link>
            <sparkle:version>15</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.5.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# Kiki 0.5.0

Kiki can now create natural speech in your own voice without sending your recording, text, or generated audio to the cloud.

## Voice Studio

- Record one guided 30–60 second reference passage with consent and live quality checks.
- Download an optional 2 GB Qwen3-TTS voice engine optimized for Apple silicon.
- Type or paste a script and generate speech entirely on your Mac.
- Generate longer writing in natural sections, cancel work in progress, and play the result in Kiki.
- Export generated speech as lossless WAV or compact M4A with AI-generation provenance metadata.
- Remove the model or your voice reference independently while keeping exported audio under your control.

## Reliability and polish

- Fixed the shared custom-button hit test so General Settings, Studio navigation, and action buttons receive ordinary mouse clicks across their full visible bounds.
- Improved disabled-button contrast in both light and dark appearance.
- Added a polished Voice Studio launch experience and a new menu-bar feature entry.

The normal transcription path is unchanged. Voice generation uses a separate native MLX pipeline and does not reduce dictation speed or quality.
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/templetongroup/Kiki/releases/download/v0.5.0/Kiki-0.5.0-macOS.zip" length="51227381" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="fQl3slRHffFRkpV6FmJAHg7vjZR9uxwM4rUHTak2HN69OdEu3wOQJ1qr7QM1w/g9D3FfCY3VAfFfuEh8PIwMCg=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>0.4.6</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:08:42 -0400</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/templetongroup/Kiki/releases/tag/v0.4.6</link>
            <sparkle:version>14</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# Kiki 0.4.6

This release fixes mouse interaction across Kiki’s custom navigation controls.

## What’s fixed

- Sidebar buttons now respond to ordinary mouse clicks throughout Settings.
- Personalization Studio navigation receives the same shared correction.
- Custom action and information buttons no longer allow their clicks to be interpreted as window dragging.
- Sidebar controls respond on the first click even when their window was previously inactive.

The root cause was a hit-test coordinate mismatch: parent-space mouse positions were being compared with local button bounds. Keyboard and accessibility activation worked, but physical clicks on later sidebar rows were rejected.

Transcription speed, quality, and Kiki’s fully local privacy model remain unchanged.
]]></description>
